Track 1: Ball Lightning Swallows the Montuno
- Story & Context: During an emergency broadcast in the heart of Hurricane Floyd’s outer bands, Silvio Canto accidentally struck his cello’s bridge with an unshielded copper grounding wire while running an intricate timba pattern through his tape delay. The ensuing electrical surge caused the station’s transmitters to blast an unintended burst of syncopated, tape-distorted dembow across every household receiver on the island, interrupting the evacuation order with a strange, hypnotic chamber groove. Listeners sheltered under tin roofs sat in stunned silence as Silvio’s panicked voice leaked through the open studio microphone, shouting over the arcing console: "When the sky opens its mouth, do not touch the copper." The broadcast ended with the explosive pop of a blown transformer, cementing the pirate station's legend across the county before the first floodwaters even crested the docks.
